{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Voice</b> — Because he mentioned that judgment shall be done, he began to rebuke Israel for not executing justice in weight and measure, and the meaning is for the city of Samaria or for Jerusalem." "<b>And sound wisdom</b> — It lacks איש (man), like ואני תפלה (and I am prayer), and the one who fears in his heart — this is the man whom the Name calls, and so it is: ואיש תושיה יראה (and a man of sound wisdom shall see), and he knows the Name mentioned. And Japheth said: the he is in place of the yod, and the meaning is that sound wisdom shall teach those who fear the Name — and this is vanity." "<b>Hear, O rod</b> — That the Name brings to chastise those who act crookedly, and know who has appointed it and will not delay. And rod is feminine, also masculine; and many nouns are like this."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:11.887749883Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}